<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<CustomObject xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        Acquisitions gap-fix, Item 5(d) (2026-08-30, Q5 option (i) in
        agent-output/design-requirements.md §0.5/§2). Moves the Call for Offers reminder
        ladder's rung values out of CallForOffersService.ALERT_INTERVALS ({7, 3, 1, 0}) and
        into configuration. The ladder itself is preserved EXACTLY - only the four values move
        here. No regression, no marker invalidation, per Q5.

        A SEPARATE TYPE FROM Stage_Threshold_Def__mdt (Item 4), DELIBERATELY - do not merge
        them if a future change looks like it would simplify things:
          1. Different cardinality/meaning: one row per STAGE (Item 4) vs one row per RUNG
             (here). A shared type would need a discriminator column plus two mutually
             irrelevant columns per row.
          2. Different readers: StageDelayService vs CallForOffersService, two unrelated
             batches.
          3. DECISIVE: the rung values are a DATA CONTRACT with existing rows.
             Opportunity.Offer_Alert_Last_Interval__c stores the rung on every deal that has
             ever alerted. Item 4's thresholds have no stored counterpart on any record. One
             shared type would let an admin edit to one feature's config silently corrupt the
             other feature's stored markers.

        ORDER IS LOAD-BEARING. CallForOffersService.intervalFor iterates its interval list and
        keeps the LAST match, which only yields "the smallest rung the deal still qualifies
        for" because that list is DESCENDING. Custom Metadata's getAll() returns a Map with NO
        guaranteed iteration order, so the accessor reading this type MUST sort
        Days_Before_Due__c descending explicitly after reading it - do not rely on record
        order in Setup or on getAll()'s Map order.

        RECORDS ARE NOT DEPLOYABLE HERE. .forceignore excludes **/customMetadata/** in this
        org (file-based CMDT record deploy throws UNKNOWN_EXCEPTION - see
        Broker_Protection_Config__mdt's own header for the same trap). This file (the TYPE)
        and its fields/*.field-meta.xml ARE deployed normally; the four rung records
        ({7, 3, 1, 0}, matching ALERT_INTERVALS byte-for-byte) are loaded by an Apex script
        (scripts/load-cfo-alert-rungs.apex - developer-owned, not part of this admin build),
        following the load-broker-protection-config.apex pattern.

        See agent-output/design-requirements.md §2 ITEM 5(d) and §10 (admin prompt, 5C) for
        the full design context.
    -->
    <label>CFO Alert Rung</label>
    <pluralLabel>CFO Alert Rungs</pluralLabel>
    <visibility>Public</visibility>
</CustomObject>
